  (text "U750: reverse blocking is always active; 3.32k ILM gives ~1 A breaker threshold, NOT a 1 A load rating. Controller allocation remains 0.5 A.\nITIMER intentionally open for minimum blanking. OC/thermal latch recovery requires removing power; ACK/ARM cannot reset this device.\nPOWER_INTERFACE_OK qualifies both driver wake and retained acknowledgement. P_ALIVE reports this qualification through a separate buffer.\nOVLO nominal 5.28 V is a cutoff threshold, not an output clamp. Worst-case threshold, transient overshoot and controller absolute limits need coordination.\nPG and reverse-blocking timing, output discharge, cable inductance, inrush and 5 V drop require physical validation. No powered mating."
    (at 25 260 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "a2ebe281-169c-419d-a283-8bdf1735e3c6")
  )
